@@ -2152,3 +2152,15 @@ Yehuda chose a fixed reviewer code over codes emailed to him (Apple reviews at n
 - **Names** need at least one letter, in any script (not "---", "1234" or emoji alone). A typed name that reaches its length limit says so under the box.
 - **Stop emails pages** say "Done" only when the link's email really is on the stop list, never for "?done=1" on its own.
 - **Give links to a campaign** say "We couldn't find that campaign" for an unknown one; "has ended" only for a campaign that really ended.
+
+## 22/11/2026: a weekly email to charities' teams, every Monday
+
+Yehuda chose (22/11/2026):
+- **Who:** a charity's owners and admins, unless they switch it off for themselves. Other team members (finance, fundraiser, viewer) only when they switch it on for themselves. Each person's choice is per charity, stored on their team row (`charity_admins.weekly_email`; empty means the role decides). Only approved (live) charities: never a draft, one waiting for review, one sent back or one suspended.
+- **When:** Monday morning, from the existing daily job (08:15 Johannesburg), no new scheduled job. It covers Monday 00:00 to Sunday 23:59 Johannesburg time of the week before. The daily job has one minute for everything, so the weekly email goes last in it; anyone it had no time for gets the same week's email on Tuesday or Wednesday (Claude's choice, so a cut-off Monday never silently drops a charity). From Thursday that week is left.
+- **What:** subject "Your week on Givezy: R3 400 from 12 gifts" ("Your week on Givezy" in a quiet week). Received, paid gifts, donors, new monthly donations, monthly donations stopped or paused, and gifts waiting for an s18A receipt (only for charities that issue them), counted exactly as the dashboard counts them: what is left of each paid gift after part refunds, a gift refunded in full is no gift, and never the contribution to Givezy or the card charge. The week before, only when it had gifts, as plain figures ("The week before: R2 100 from 8 gifts."), never a percentage or "up/down". One button, "Open your dashboard". Never a donor's name, address, ID number or amount per donor.
+- **Quiet weeks:** still sent, short: "No gifts came in last week." with one next step (add a logo and cover photo, then tell donors what you do, then share your page). No guilt wording, no impact figure.
+- **Stopping it:** the footer says why they get it and links to "Switch off the weekly email" (`/weekly-email/stop`, a single-purpose link that asks first and switches off only that person's email for that charity; a mail app's own Unsubscribe does the same through `/api/stop/weekly`). Anyone on the team switches theirs on or off on the dashboard's Team page ("Your weekly email"); pressing it again is the undo.
+- **Never twice:** each email's row in `charity_weekly_emails` (charity, person, the week's Monday) is written before it is sent; the database refuses a second one. A send that surely didn't go is released and tried the next day; one that may have gone is never repeated.
+- **Switch:** `WEEKLY_CHARITY_EMAIL=yes` on the server, off by default; `EMAIL_ALLOWLIST` still applies on the test site. Migration `20261122000003_charity_weekly_email.sql`; without it nothing is sent and one log line says so.
+- Built in `src/lib/charity/weekly-summary.ts` (week, figures, words) and `weekly-summary-store.ts` (reads, send log, stop link). Wording is DRAFT for Yehuda to read in a real inbox (it is in the sample emails, Admin, Settings).
